# TeraLab

TeraLab is a self-hosted network lab platform. It designs, runs and saves
topologies built from QEMU, Cisco IOL, Dynamips and VPCS nodes, with a Vue
web UI, a PHP API and a Go agent that owns the engine processes.

TeraLab is derived from UNetLab 1.0.2-2 and is licensed AGPL-3.0-or-later.
See `PROVENANCE.md`, `NOTICE` and `LICENSES/` for the lineage and the
third-party licences.

## Requirements

- Debian 13 (trixie) with Apache 2.4 and PHP 8.4 (`pdo_sqlite`, `mbstring`)
- Go 1.22+ to build the agent
- Node 20+ to build the web UI
- QEMU/KVM (`qemu-system-x86_64`, `qemu-img`)

Cisco IOL and Dynamips are separate programs: TeraLab never redistributes
vendor images, IOS files or IOU/`iourc` credentials. Users supply those.

## Install

```sh
sudo packaging/teralab/install.sh
```

The installer is idempotent, keeps `/etc/teralab` and `/var/lib/teralab`,
and is the supported upgrade path. See `docs/INSTALL.md` and
`docs/UPGRADE.md`.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `api/` | PHP 8.4 Slim API (v2 plus the v1 compatibility adapter) |
| `agent/` | Go agent: engines, port mapping, console gateway |
| `ui/` | Vue 3 + Vite web UI |
| `html/` | Document root: Vue build, templates, icons and the About page |
| `packaging/` | Installer and the separate Dynamips package build |
| `scripts/` | CI, release and development gates |
| `tests/` | Shared CI configuration |
| `docs/` | Published user documentation |

## Tests

```sh
cd api && composer test && composer stan
cd agent && go test ./...
cd ui && npm test && npm run build
```

Release gates:

```sh
./scripts/teralab-project-init.sh --check
./scripts/check-artifact-policy.sh
./scripts/check-licence-headers.sh
./scripts/check-secrets.sh
```

## Documentation

- `docs/INSTALL.md` — installation and first-run setup
- `docs/API.md` — API quick reference; `docs/openapi.yaml` — OpenAPI draft
- `docs/LAB-FORMAT.md` — the portable `.unl` lab format and EVE-NG import
- `docs/AGENT.md` — agent protocol and engine behaviour
- `docs/SECURITY.md` — security model
- `docs/SBOM.md` — dependency inventory

